<section class="fragment-benchmark" data-artifact="benchmark" data-slice="tempo-and-restarts" data-mode="baseline">
  <!-- @include-skip the metric table is hand-inlined as in the prior revisions of this artifact -->
  <table class="bm-metrics">
    <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Baseline (bce0144)</th><th>Tripwire</th><th>Unit</th><th>Direction</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr data-role="gate"><td>bench.cpu_us_per_tick</td><td>1.5519</td><td>1.7071</td><td>us</td><td>lower is better</td><td>gate</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="gate"><td>bench.peak_mem_mb</td><td>6.840</td><td>8.55</td><td>MB</td><td>lower is better</td><td>gate</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>bench.cpu_ms_per_match</td><td>443.6</td><td>reported (488.0)</td><td>ms</td><td>lower is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>bench.match_wall_ms</td><td>448</td><td>budget 2000</td><td>ms</td><td>lower is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>bench.ticks_per_match</td><td>285850</td><td>at most 360000</td><td>ticks</td><td>lower is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>engine.ticks_per_s</td><td>638058</td><td>none</td><td>ticks/s</td><td>higher is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>criterion.tick_step_us</td><td>1.5786</td><td>none</td><td>us</td><td>lower is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>criterion.steering_pass_22_ns</td><td>864.72</td><td>none</td><td>ns</td><td>lower is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="report"><td>bench.stream_ticks_per_s</td><td>440037</td><td>none</td><td>ticks/s</td><td>higher is better</td><td>reported</td></tr>
      <tr data-role="gate"><td>bench.stream_peak_mem_mb</td><td>8.355</td><td>10.44</td><td>MB</td><td>lower is better</td><td>stream gate</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">The gate is per tick</div><div class="callout-body">The slice adds a carry window to the carrier's decision, longer restart delays, and a clearance check that runs only while a fast pass is inside a penalty area. It names no tripwire, so the default rule applies: +10 percent processor time per tick and +25 percent peak memory. Processor time per match is reported beside it.</div></aside>

  <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">Dead-ball ticks cost less</div><div class="callout-body">Longer restarts turn live ticks into dead-ball ticks, which are cheaper. The per-tick mean can fall for that reason alone. Such a fall is not an improvement of the code.</div></aside>

  <style>
    .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics th, .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.25); }
    .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics tr[data-role="gate"] td:first-child { font-weight: 600; }
    .fragment-benchmark .callout { margin-top: 12px; }
  </style>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-benchmark');
      var metrics = root ? root.querySelectorAll('.bm-metrics tbody tr').length : 0;
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', { detail: { name: 'benchmark', artifact: 'benchmark', counts: { metrics: metrics, regressions: 0, improvements: 0 } } }));
    })();
  </script>
</section>
